  "title": "Gov. Stitt Surveys Tornado Damage",
  "description": "Okla. Governor Kevin Stitt visited Bryan County, Okla., May 6, 2019. The Okla. National Guard supported the Governor during his visit to Bryan County, Okla., as he assessed storm damage where an F-3 tornado destroyed homes and took the lives of two Oklahomans. Stitt declared a state of emergency for 52 counties that were effected by these storms that took place on April 30. The National Weather Service says at least 16 tornados were reported across the state that day.",
